{"name":"Steamed Salmon","hex":"#ee8888","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steamed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Heated and processed by steam, such as being cooked by steaming.","Angry; hot under the collar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of steam"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steamed"},{"term":"salmon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several species of fish, typically of the Salmoninae subfamily, brownish above with silvery sides and delicate pinkish-orange flesh; they ascend rivers to spawn.","A meal or dish made from this fish."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale pinkish-orange colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steaming","blocks":[{"text":"Steaming is a method of cooking using steam. In steaming, the food is fully immersed in steam, with no air present, so that the steam condenses on the food, and then the condensate drips down away from the food. This is often achieved in a food steamer, a kitchen appliance made specifically to cook food with steam, but food can also be steamed in a wok. In the American Southwest, steam pits used for cooking have been found dating back about 5,000 years. Steaming is considered a healthy cooking technique that can be used for many kinds of foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Steaming_rice.jpg/330px-Steaming_rice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steaming","wikidata":"Q1415859"},{"title":"Salmon","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon are any of several commercially important species of ray-finned fish that can live in either freshwater or saltwater from the genera Salmo and Oncorhynchus of the family Salmonidae, native to tributaries of the North Atlantic (Salmo) and North Pacific (Oncorhynchus) basins. Salmon is a colloquial or common name used for fish in this group, but is not a scientific name. Other closely related fish in the same family include trout, char, grayling, whitefish, lenok and taimen, all coldwater fish of the subarctic and cooler temperate regions with some sporadic endorheic populations in Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Salmo_salar.jpg/330px-Salmo_salar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon","wikidata":"Q2796766"},{"title":"Salmon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon is a warm color ranging from light orange to pink, named after the color of salmon flesh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg/330px-SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2015138"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/HK_TKL_%E8%AA%BF%E6%99%AF%E5%B6%BA_Tiu_Keng_Leng_%E9%83%BD%E6%9C%83%E9%A7%85_Metro_Town_Shopping_Mall_shop_%E8%B1%AA%E5%AE%B4%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Ho_Yin_Seafood_Restaurant_December_2019_SS2_dim_sum_take-away_food_counter.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/HK_TKL_%E8%AA%BF%E6%99%AF%E5%B6%BA_Tiu_Keng_Leng_%E9%83%BD%E6%9C%83%E9%A7%85_Metro_Town_Shopping_Mall_shop_%E8%B1%AA%E5%AE%B4%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Ho_Yin_Seafood_Restaurant_December_2019_SS2_dim_sum_take-away_food_counter.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/HK_TKL_%E8%AA%BF%E6%99%AF%E5%B6%BA_Tiu_Keng_Leng_%E9%83%BD%E6%9C%83%E9%A7%85_Metro_Town_Shopping_Mall_shop_%E8%B1%AA%E5%AE%B4%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%8